`; an entity-level action counts for every stage). Entry, exit and subscription bodies are never cleared, and a transition there is an unguarded entry. An observed flow has no action and no stage, so no guard site clears it. An allowance naming a reported `DMEFF014` is the `DMALW002` error and consumes nothing. An allowance no analysis arm consumed (wrong code or path, stale after the flow became compatible, blank provenance) is the `DMALW001` error. `WithDomain` copies both lists on both branches. ADR: [`docs/decisions/2026-11-08-diagnostic-allowance.md`](decisions/2026-11-08-diagnostic-allowance.md).
 
-**Unverified writes (Q4).** Silence from a write check means verified — with one exception, below: a call-chain postcondition with no known value range. Every write to a property carrying a `range` constraint — `assign`, entry/exit and `when` bodies, and `create`/`create in` initializers (evaluated in the creator's scope, with the creating action's parameters in scope, against declared ranges only: no `require` narrowing and no stage invariants, unlike an assign) — gets exactly one `WriteVerdict`: `Satisfied` is silent and counted, `Violated` is a `DMEFF008` error ("entirely outside"), and `Undecided` is a `DMEFF008` warning when the value has a known range or length interval ("can fall outside") or a `DMCS003` warning otherwise (no usable bound, an operator the interval flow does not model, or a constraint kind with no flow decision). `ConstraintKind.WriteRelevant` is the kind's own claim that a computed value can be decided; it is set for `Range`, `Length`, `Pattern` and `Equality` (V-08a: a Text value is `Satisfied` only when its length interval — its declared `length(...)`, `[0, +∞)` for a Text with none, a `+` of such values, or a `match` over them (#1040) — is inside the target's, a pattern or `equals` only when the value carries the identical one, else `Undecided`, never `Violated`, and `poly_check` takes its verdict from `GetVerification`, so any unverified write reads `unknown`). `unique` (stored state), `required` (DMEFF014) and enum membership (the type check) are excluded, and an unregistered kind is fail-closed. A write-relevant pair is also decided on an observed flow and in the parameter arm, which compare declared bounds; the call chain (`ValidateCallChainPostconditions`) decides through the same `DecideRange` and records every non-`Satisfied` outcome through `WriteRecorder`, deduplicated per effect node (V-05b); a postcondition with no value range is still skipped silently. `WriteVerificationFacts` (`Analysis/WriteVerification.cs`) is the analysis-side record on the `Domain`: one entry per unverified write plus a `Verified` count, never one per constraint, and never "proven" while a write is unverified. `DMEFF008` itself is unchanged.
