 **Guard narrowing (V-02).** `EffectInvariantAnalyzer` narrows the abstract environment an action's effects run in by its guards (`require`'d policies, `if` conditions with their negation in the else-branch, a callee's guards and a `for … where` policy) through one refiner pair, `Refine`/`RefineNegated`: a comparison of a property with a literal (either side) or with another property (a relation), `and`, `or` (the hull of the arms; a dead arm is skipped, both dead leave the environment as it came in, and no relation is recorded inside an arm) and `not` (the complement; De Morgan over `and`/`or`); any other leaf narrows nothing, positively or negated. Integrality comes from `DomainTypeModelMetadata` (read at the Domain node, failing closed when absent): on a property whose `KindOf(OfProperty(p))` is `Integer64`, `x < v` is `x <= ceil(v) - 1` and `x > v` is `x >= floor(v) + 1`, and `x != v` moves an endpoint equal to an integral `v` in by one; on any other axis a strict bound stays inclusive (OQ-5) and `!=` narrows nothing. A point range `x != v` is empty on any axis. The integral set is per entity, so a callee's guard uses the callee entity's. Ranges describe present values: a comparison is false for a null value except `!=`, so a leaf that holds for null (a positive `!=` or a negated comparison) narrows an optional property's present values but never empties it, nor keeps a relation that would contradict it. A guard no value satisfies is the existing unsatisfiable-precondition error (`DMCS001`). **Policy guard facts (V-18).** `PolicyGuardFacts` (`Poly/DomainModeling/Analysis/PolicyGuardFacts.cs`, internal) is the one seam through which a `require`'d policy narrows the environment, at action entry and on a self, cross-entity or fan-out invoke: `Guards(action, stage)` lists the action's policies (its `require not P` markers included) and the stage's, except a stage policy the action negates, whose gate the lowered body suppresses (`EmitStagePolicyGuards`); `EffectAnalyzer`'s exit-block target check reads that list too: an entity-level hop whose action requires a policy the stage requires the negation of is refused before any effect runs, so it is not a hop that leaves the stage (`DMEFF017`, #802). `Refine` narrows by one guard, a `not_P` marker by the owner's policy `P` found by name (as the runtime calls it) and negated once, never the marker's own expression, and narrows nothing when the owner has no `P`. F-09 supplies only a `PolicyInstantiator` delegate and the arguments; arguments with no instantiator throw. `CollectPreconditions` stays the public precondition and export set (`ActionStageInvariant.Preconditions`, `InternalDomainProducer.ExportPreconditions`). Create and create-in initializers read the walk's environment at the create (`ActionStageInvariant.InitializerValues`, the context action's own creates only), which `EffectAnalyzer.ValidateInitializerValue` decides per stage context; the environment is trusted for an initializer only while every effect on that path is one the walk models (assign, `if`, composite, an entered self-invoke), so a create in or after a loop, after a transition, a cross-entity or fan-out invoke, a create or a create-in (it can notify a subscription on the creator), and a context with no record, keep the declared-range path (#863 owns the loop environment). An assign recorded on such a path takes its value from a second walk over `PolicyGuardFacts.PreconditionGuards` (the guards before V-18: no `require not`, no stage-gate lift), so this narrowing never composes with the loop or write-back environment into a new clean.
 
